00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:39.360
or this bacteria's DNA, bacterial
cell's DNA, and some RNA.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.300
And so, this is what's inside a protein.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.970
And so what protein biochemists wanna do

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.150
or what they do is they study

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:47.660
each of these individual proteins.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.113
They study their function.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.910
And so the reason is,
each of these proteins

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.283
are in such close contact
with other proteins,

00:06:55.283 --> 00:06:58.227
so they actually work with other proteins.

00:06:58.227 --> 00:07:01.510
So, just imagine each of
these circles is a protein

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:02.840
and each of these lines mean

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.300
there's proteins
interacting with each other

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.940
and so, protein biochemists
study the interactions

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:12.150
between proteins to understand
how bacteria survive

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:16.230
or how particular
functions inside bacteria

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:18.457
help them to cause disease.

00:07:18.457 --> 00:07:22.270
