00:51:34.900 --> 00:51:38.030
is a synthesis reaction that's happening.

00:51:38.030 --> 00:51:41.210
So you have the protein,

00:51:41.210 --> 00:51:42.510
and you put the protein

00:51:44.170 --> 00:51:46.540
in a solution with a particular dye

00:51:46.540 --> 00:51:48.550
that only binds to protein.

00:51:48.550 --> 00:51:50.943
And that dye, when it binds to protein,

00:51:52.680 --> 00:51:55.010
it becomes this protein dye

00:51:56.020 --> 00:51:58.600
combination which releases a blue color.

00:51:58.600 --> 00:52:00.960
And that's just specific to the dye.

00:52:00.960 --> 00:52:05.560
The dye, when it binds to
protein, it releases a particular,

00:52:05.560 --> 00:52:08.170
it changes state and it
produces a blue color.

00:52:08.170 --> 00:52:11.220
And so that's a synthesis
chemical reaction

00:52:11.220 --> 00:52:12.940
that's occurring.

00:52:12.940 --> 00:52:16.390
And so, yeah, so the
more protein you have,

00:52:16.390 --> 00:52:18.180
the more dye can react

00:52:18.180 --> 00:52:20.300
and then produce that
blue color that you saw.

00:52:20.300 --> 00:52:22.950
That's why you have more blue

00:52:22.950 --> 00:52:25.700
in the presence of a
greater amount of protein.

