00:58:37.991 --> 00:58:40.550
- So green fluorescent protein,

00:58:40.550 --> 00:58:41.830
the way that it fluoresces,

00:58:41.830 --> 00:58:44.040
is not due to a chemical reaction,

00:58:44.040 --> 00:58:47.530
but when you change its
environment with chemicals,

00:58:47.530 --> 00:58:49.640
the chemicals then react with the protein

00:58:49.640 --> 00:58:52.540
to form their own
chemical reactions, right?

00:58:52.540 --> 00:58:54.873
And so that's why when you add the acid,

00:58:56.330 --> 00:58:58.550
something happens, a
chemical reaction takes place

00:58:58.550 --> 00:58:59.810
with the green fluorescent protein

00:58:59.810 --> 00:59:01.810
which makes it stop fluorescing,

00:59:01.810 --> 00:59:03.423
and then when you add the base,

00:59:05.791 --> 00:59:10.433
this solution here, it changed
the chemical environment

00:59:10.433 --> 00:59:12.910
that the green fluorescent protein within,

00:59:12.910 --> 00:59:15.920
and then it restored back the
fluorescence of the protein.

00:59:15.920 --> 00:59:18.950
So I'm just gonna sh...

00:59:18.950 --> 00:59:20.743
So let's see what's going on there.

